# Post-Change Test Hook

Whenever you finish a command where **files have been created, saved, or deleted**, do the following **before returning to the user**:

## Workflow

**Order is mandatory:** run **ESLint** (step 1) and resolve problems **before** starting **any** Vitest run (step 2). Do not run `npx vitest` or `npm run test` until `npm run lint` has finished and **errors** are fixed (warnings: fix when the project treats them as blocking, or when trivial).

1. **Run ESLint and fix lint errors**:
   - If the project has a lint script: run **`npm run lint`** (this repo: **`eslint .`**) and fix any reported **errors**.
   - If there is no lint script: run the editor linter (e.g. ReadLints) on changed files and fix any reported errors.

2. **Run tests in two passes** (Vitest) — only **after** step 1 succeeds; skip when **Skills only — no Vitest** (below) applies.
   - **Pass A (scoped — change set):** `npx vitest run --changed` runs tests Vitest associates with git **uncommitted** changes (staged and unstaged), i.e. the usual “this edit batch” before commit. If the working tree is **clean** (changes were already committed), run `npx vitest run --changed HEAD~1` instead so Pass A still targets tests affected by the **latest commit**.
   - **Pass B (full suite):** `npm run test` (`npx vitest run`).

3. **If all tests pass**:
   - Return your normal response to the user
   - At the end, append: `All (#) tests have passed` (replace # with the actual count)

4. **If any tests fail**:
   - Attempt to fix the failing tests
   - Re-run **`npm run lint`** (ESLint), then **Pass A then Pass B** (scoped `npx vitest run --changed` or `… --changed HEAD~1` when appropriate, then `npm run test`)
   - Repeat up to **2 fix attempts** total
   - If tests pass after a fix: return with `All (#) tests have passed` as above
   - If tests still fail after 2 attempts: stop fixing, return to the user with your response and at the end say in **red text**: `<span style="color: red">(#) tests failed</span>` (replace # with the failure count). Use this exact phrasing so the failure is clearly visible.

## When to Skip

- Skip this hook if **no files** were created, saved, or deleted during the command
- Skip for purely informational or exploratory requests (e.g. "what does X do?", "explain Y")
- Skip when the only modified files are planning documents (e.g. files under `Plans/` or standalone plan/design markdown docs) and no code/runtime/config files changed

### Skills only — no Vitest

If the **only** files you created, saved, or deleted in that command are under **`.cursor/skills/`** (e.g. editing `SKILL.md`):

- **Do not** run Vitest (neither `--changed` / scoped nor `npm run test`).
- **Do not** append `All (#) tests have passed` or the red tests-failed footer (the suite was not run).
- **`npm run lint`**: optional; skip it when nothing outside `.cursor/skills/` changed.
